<http://data.silknow.org/object/8b9eb304-dfbf-3fc9-ba21-cb073fa1b448>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "In the early to mid-nineteenth century, cream or white silk waistcoats were popular for wedding wear. They were often embroidered, sometimes by family members or even by the future bride. A hand-written paper label sewn into this waistcoat links it to the marriage of John Montefiore and Julia Norman on the 28th January 1845. We have the white and silver figured silk waistcoat that John wore for the ceremony (see T.668-1919), so perhaps this waistcoat was embroidered by Julia as a wedding gift for her new husband.\n\nThe choice of forget-me-nots, which signify fidelity, would have been appropriate for a wedding waistcoat. John and Julia Montefiore's marriage lasted 50 years, ending only with their deaths in 1895."@en , "White silk waistcoat embroidered with coloured silks and copper-gilt thread; a regularly spaced sprig motif of small blue forget-me-nots. Lined in pinkish cotton, 6 covered buttons down the front and turned-over collar."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e5a51d2c-1a6e-3552-a1f9-9ba746f17b7d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ddb3178a-5638-39d1-8fa2-56a48d9582dc> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/bde7b0c8-e6b9-350a-97a2-69c95bdb4f0d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/7d5d87d1-21c5-3cdc-8558-1a0d76a241ac> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/beff9f70-900d-30d2-b578-7346b8fda34e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "White silk waistcoat embroidered with coloured silks and copper-gilt thread; a regularly spaced sprig motif of small blue forget-me-nots. Lined in pinkish cotton, 6 covered buttons down the front and turned-over collar."@en , "In the early to mid-nineteenth century, cream or white silk waistcoats were popular for wedding wear. They were often embroidered, sometimes by family members or even by the future bride. A hand-written paper label sewn into this waistcoat links it to the marriage of John Montefiore and Julia Norman on the 28th January 1845. We have the white and silver figured silk waistcoat that John wore for the ceremony (see T.668-1919), so perhaps this waistcoat was embroidered by Julia as a wedding gift for her new husband.\n\nThe choice of forget-me-nots, which signify fidelity, would have been appropriate for a wedding waistcoat. John and Julia Montefiore's marriage lasted 50 years, ending only with their deaths in 1895."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/8b9eb304-dfbf-3fc9-ba21-cb073fa1b448/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/8b9eb304-dfbf-3fc9-ba21-cb073fa1b448/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.669-1919" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O230679> .

